---
deadlock_detection: false
---

# session_title_history: who writes history's title for one session, and
# what they must never do to each other (go/tests/model/README.md). The
# other half, the name as serve and the pages show it, is
# specs/session_title_writers.fizz; they meet at history's title (hist).
#
# Checked against:
#   live   plugins/title/title.go: after every finished turn the Titler
#          (under its work mutex) logs the turn ("turn-summary", one small
#          model call) and then names the session once ("title" with
#          final: true, a second call) unless a final name exists; then it
#          arms the quiet timer (the main model's cache window). quiet
#          names it if no turn is open; shutdown cancels an in-flight call
#          and makes one last log + name attempt under a 10 s deadline.
#          Until a final name exists readers show the opening line
#          (plugins/history List: the last "title" entry wins, else the
#          first input's first line): the provisional name.
#   cli    plugins/title/summarize.go backfillOne (`bough summarize`):
#          reads the file, skips it if it has any turn-summary, else logs
#          the finished turns and names the session, then OpenExisting +
#          Append + Close.
#   file   plugins/history: Store.Append writes each line under an
#          exclusive flock and catchUp only raises seq past foreign lines,
#          it never adopts them into Entries(); OpenExisting's
#          dropTornTail truncates the file after its last newline, with no
#          flock.
#   serve  a restart or an archive SIGKILLs the child (supervisor.go
#          killChild): no shutdown naming, the timer and any call die.
#
# The spec says what the design must be; where the code today differs it
# says so under DIVERGES, and this flow's model tests turn it red:
#
# DIVERGES 1 (double final). The live Titler decides "already named"
#   from its own Entries(), which never include lines another process
#   appended, and backfillOne decides "not yet summarized" from a read
#   taken before its model calls, re-checked by nothing. `bough summarize`
#   on a live session therefore writes a final name, and the live Titler
#   writes a second (or the other way round); the name flips to the
#   later. The spec re-reads the file under the flock before either
#   appends a final name.
# DIVERGES 2 (torn live line). summarize's OpenExisting runs dropTornTail
#   without the flock. A live Store holds the flock across one line's
#   write + flush, and a line longer than bufio's buffer reaches the file
#   in more than one write: the half already on disk looks torn and is
#   truncated away, and the rest lands glued to nothing. The spec's
#   BackfillWrite waits for the flock (require not writing).
# DIVERGES 3 (quiet never logs). The package doc says a failed call is
#   retried by the next turn, the quiet timer or shutdown; quiet only
#   runs finalName, which needs a logged turn. When the turn's log call
#   failed, the quiet retry does nothing, and an idle live session stays
#   on its provisional name until another turn or shutdown. The spec's
#   quiet attempt logs and names, like the others.
#
# Corrections to the mapped model:
# - "A session with a logged turn eventually gets a final name unless the
#   model always fails" does not hold even with one failed call: every
#   retry is tied to an event of the live child (turn end, quiet,
#   shutdown). A child SIGKILLed by a serve restart or an archive, or one
#   whose shutdown attempt failed, leaves the session unnamed until a new
#   turn; and `bough summarize` skips it for good once any turn-summary
#   exists ("already summarized"). The liveness claim here is the one the
#   design can keep: a live child names its session, given the small model
#   answers after at most one failed call.
# - "provisional" is not an entry: nothing writes the opening line as a
#   title; it is what readers fall back to while there is no final name.
#
# Fields:
#   turn     the latest turn: "open" (running) or "done" (ended: done,
#            cancelled or failed; the Titler logs all three)
#   live     a child holds the session (its Store, its Titler)
#   job      the Titler's call in flight: "" none, "turn" (turn end),
#            "quiet" (the timer), "shutdown" (the last attempt)
#   timer    the quiet timer is armed
#   failed   the small model has failed a call (at most one: see the
#            liveness claim)
#   logged   the file holds a turn-summary
#   hist     history's title: "prompt" (provisional), "auto" (the live
#            Titler's final), "filled" (summarize's final)
#   finals   final title entries in the file
#   backfill "" or "read": `bough summarize` read the file, found nothing
#            logged, and is calling the model
#   writing  the live Store is part-way through one line (flock held)
#   torn     a live line was cut by another writer

role Session:
    # A session whose first turn is running: its name is the opening line.
    action Init:
        self.turn = "open"
        self.live = True
        self.job = ""
        self.timer = False
        self.failed = False
        self.logged = False
        self.hist = "prompt"
        self.finals = 0
        self.backfill = ""
        self.writing = False
        self.torn = False

    # The turn ends; the Titler's turnDone takes the work mutex (a call
    # already in flight goes first).
    atomic fair<strong> action TurnDone:
        require self.live and self.turn == "open" and self.job == ""
        self.turn = "done"
        self.timer = False
        self.job = "turn"

    # The person sends another prompt; serve resumes a session with no
    # child (`-r <id>`). An open turn makes a firing quiet timer do
    # nothing, so it is as good as disarmed.
    atomic action Prompt:
        require self.turn == "done" and self.job != "shutdown"
        self.turn = "open"
        self.live = True
        self.timer = False

    # The small model answers: the turn is logged and, if the file has no
    # final name yet (re-read under the flock: DIVERGES 1), the session is
    # named. Store.Append serialises with a line in progress.
    atomic fair<strong> action SmallModelOk:
        require self.job != "" and not self.writing
        if self.finals == 0:
            self.hist = "auto"
            self.finals = self.finals + 1
        self.logged = True
        if self.job == "shutdown":
            self.live = False
        self.timer = False
        self.job = ""

    # A call fails (error, timeout, cancelled by the deadline): the log
    # call, or the name call after the log landed. A turn's attempt still
    # arms the quiet timer.
    atomic action SmallModelFails:
        require self.job != "" and not self.failed
        self.failed = True
        self.logged = any [self.logged, True]
        if self.job == "turn":
            self.timer = True
        if self.job == "shutdown":
            self.live = False
        self.job = ""

    # A cache window passed with no turn open: log and name again
    # (DIVERGES 3: the code only names).
    atomic fair<strong> action QuietTimer:
        require self.live and self.timer and self.job == "" and self.turn == "done"
        self.timer = False
        self.job = "quiet"

    # The child closes (the person quits, headless input ends): an open
    # turn ends cancelled, an in-flight call is cancelled, and shutdown
    # makes the last attempt.
    atomic action ChildShutdown:
        require self.live and self.job != "shutdown"
        self.turn = "done"
        self.timer = False
        self.job = "shutdown"

    # serve restarts or archives the session: SIGKILL. The call, the timer
    # and a half-written line die with the child (the next opener drops
    # that torn tail: nobody is appending to it any more).
    atomic action ChildKilled:
        require self.live
        self.live = False
        self.turn = "done"
        self.job = ""
        self.timer = False
        self.writing = False

    # The live Store starts one long line (an assistant entry, a tool
    # result) and finishes it.
    atomic action LiveWriteStart:
        require self.live and not self.writing
        self.writing = True

    atomic fair<strong> action LiveWriteEnd:
        require self.writing
        self.writing = False

    # `bough summarize` reads the file: a finished turn and no
    # turn-summary, so it calls the model.
    atomic action SummarizeRead:
        require self.backfill == "" and self.turn == "done" and not self.logged
        self.backfill = "read"

    # Its calls answered: it opens the file for append and writes. It
    # takes the flock first (DIVERGES 2) and re-reads the file under it
    # (DIVERGES 1): a final name written meanwhile is kept.
    atomic fair<strong> action SummarizeWrite:
        require self.backfill == "read" and not self.writing
        if self.finals == 0:
            self.hist = "filled"
            self.finals = self.finals + 1
        self.logged = True
        self.backfill = ""

action Init:
    session = Session()

# At most one final title entry per session, across processes.
always assertion AtMostOneFinal:
    return session.finals <= 1

# No writer cuts bytes a live writer is appending.
always assertion NoTornLiveLine:
    return not session.torn

# The opening line is the name exactly until a final name is written.
always assertion ProvisionalUntilFinal:
    return (session.hist == "prompt") == (session.finals == 0)

# A live child names its session, given the small model answers after at
# most one failed call.
always eventually assertion LiveSessionGetsNamed:
    return session.finals > 0 or not session.live
